.scratch/

# An assistant's request body for the Supabase management API, written to the
# repo root instead of held in memory. There is no Supabase CLI and no
# service-role key on this machine, so the only route to DDL on tdg-core is
# POST /v1/projects/<ref>/database/query with the SQL as a JSON field — and
# `{"q": "<the whole migration>"}` is that body, saved to a file. It reappears
# on the next apply, which is why this is an ignore rather than a delete.
#
# It carries no credential: the bearer token is a header at call time and the
# file has one key. It is ignored because it is 26KB of duplicated SQL sitting
# where a reflex `git add -A` would take it, and this repo has had exactly that
# happen — 850 lines of a concurrent session's half-built console went into a
# commit about the Store. **The real fix is to write it to the session
# scratchpad under %TEMP%, not here**; this line only stops it landing.
/x.json

# DevFleet Logbook version history
.devfleet/logbook/.history/

# DevFleet Logbook trash
.devfleet/logbook/.trash/

# Supabase CLI scratch (regenerates on every CLI run)
supabase/.temp/
